Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 01:57:28 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 100/230] Close the last micro-interactions: score roll-up, win
 confetti, toasts, pull ring
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The score header snapped from one number to the next; it now rolls up with the
same CountUp the tables use, so a goal lands instead of jumping.

A pick that pays off is the one moment this app can celebrate, and the user is
already on the match when it resolves, so a win fires the existing confetti
burst. The fire-once rule lives in src/lib/predictionWin.ts and is tested: the
first payload of a session only seeds the status map, so opening an
already-resolved match celebrates nothing and a settled pick never re-fires.

Toasts drop in from above the header and leave upward, and the tone now owns a
4px accent bar on the card's leading edge (border-s-4, so it flips in Persian)
over the existing 1px tone border — a card rather than a pill, since an accent
bar needs a straight edge to sit on.

The pull-to-refresh indicator is a ball turning inside a volt ring that fills
with the drag and closes at the threshold, instead of a generic spinner.

